{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8b2a37010bbe5fdd993a1864c3ee79b477267d2746943c2795315b668fd28d94","digest":{"component_or_area":"compaction sweep","key_entities":["_compact_locked","_build_authorship_ledger","build_ticket_position_commit_map","authorship.build_position_commit_map","_commit_backfill","compact_all_cli","compact_txn.py","compact.py","compact_trigger.run_sweep","write_lock_is_busy","_sweep_position_map","_run_sweep","_sweep_should_yield","_sweep_one_ticket"],"problem_keywords":["store lock stall","sweep performance","git history walk","compaction","store-wide sweep","critical section","writer starvation"],"propositions":["The store-wide compaction sweep spawns one full git log --full-history walk per ticket inside the store write lock, holding all writers for minutes at a time.","Per-ticket history walks are redundant; a position-keyed map built once per sweep and consulted per-ticket removes N walks from the critical section.","The sweep never re-yields mid-run; write_lock_is_busy is probed once before starting, leaving writers to block for the entire duration.","The sweep stages all uncommitted paths with git add -A instead of scoped add, allowing concurrent in-flight event files to be swept into the compaction commit.","Hoisting the history walk and position map outside the lock, with scoped staging and mid-run re-yield, eliminates the lock hold from git I/O and restores responsiveness."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787653884597037001,"uuid":"0178866a-a696-47b0-abb4-ffd88506b90d"}